{"chunk_id": "43b2b476ecfa8f6eb09b3d19137d5e63_3", "parent_id": "43b2b476ecfa8f6eb09b3d19137d5e63", "source": "darglobal", "source_url": "https://darglobal.co.uk/blog/property-investment-in-qatar-for-non-qataris", "title": "Property Investment in Qatar: A Step-by-Step Guide for Non-Qataris", "doc_type": "blog", "location": "Qatar", "content": ". As per Decision No. 28 of 2020, these areas offer full ownership rights, enabling expats to buy, sell, and lease properties without restrictions in prime locations. This law significantly expanded property ownership rights for non-Qataris. Investors purchasing properties worth QAR 730,000 or more are eligible for residency permits, while investments exceeding QAR 3.65 million may offer permanent residency-like benefits, including access to public services. 3. Real Estate Development Law Qatar's Real Estate Development Law regulates licensing, project approvals, and developer obligations. It ensures investor protection by mandating escrow accounts, clear delivery timelines, and construction standards, enhancing transparency, and reducing any risks for property investment in Qatar", "chunk_index": 3, "total_chunks": 7, "scraped_at": "2026-11-18T10:46:31.770248+00:00"}
